# Fallback Response — Decision Tree

## Introduction
When a customer's issue doesn't match order status or returns/refunds, the fallback tree takes over. It asks one triage question, then routes the customer to either a human agent or a self-serve help link — no free text, just clicks.

## The Decision Tree

```
Fallback triggered
        │
        ▼
"What best describes your need?"
        │
   ┌────┼────────┬──────────┐
   ▼    ▼        ▼          ▼
Product Billing Feedback  Not sure
/account issue             │
   │      │       │        ▼
   └──────┴───────┘   Help center link
        ▼              (no ticket created)
  Escalate to agent
  (category shared
   with the agent)
```

## What's Happening
- Product/account, Billing issue, Feedback → escalate to a human, with the chosen category attached so the agent has context
- Not sure → no ticket is created; the customer is pointed to the help center instead

This keeps the fallback consistent with the rest of the tool (button clicks only) and still deflects tickets where possible, instead of escalating everything by default.
